WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.912
Step nine dry-runs the agent Conditional
Access plan with its approved hash.

2
00:00:04.912 --> 00:00:07.156
It would send exactly one request:

3
00:00:07.156 --> 00:00:12.125
a POST to the beta Conditional Access
endpoint on the cloud's own Graph host,

4
00:00:12.125 --> 00:00:16.212
for the high-risk policy, because
the other is already in place.

5
00:00:16.212 --> 00:00:20.574
Step ten runs the same command with
the apply switch, against the fake.

6
00:00:20.574 --> 00:00:24.252
One write is sent, and the
policy is created report-only,

7
00:00:24.252 --> 00:00:29.400
with a reminder to review its report-only
results before any change of state.

8
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.163
Then you pass a hash of zeros, one
nobody approved, and the script refuses:

9
00:00:34.163 --> 00:00:39.088
the plan's hash isn't the approved one,
and it won't run a plan nobody reviewed.

10
00:00:39.088 --> 00:00:42.087
Pasted line by line,
your shell carries on.

11
00:00:42.087 --> 00:00:47.275
Step eleven runs every test: five
hundred thirteen pass, none fail.

12
00:00:47.275 --> 00:00:49.180
Then delete the output folder.
